he was the first wife of Pāṇḍu. As he was prevented by a curse from having progeny, he allowed his wife to make use of a charm she had acquired from the sage Durvāsas, by means of which she was to have a son by any god she liked to invoke. She invoked Dharma, Vāyu and Indra, and had from them Yudhiṣṭhira, Bhīma and Arjuna respectively. She was also mother of Karṇa by the deity Sun whom she invoked in her virginhood to test her charm.]", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "A fragrant resin.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "The wife of a Brāhmaṇa.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["kuntii", "kuntī"], "synonyms_slp1": ["kuntii", "kuntī"]}], "kuntr": [{"id": "kuntr", "headword": "कुन्त्र्", "headword_slp1": "kuntr", "fold": "kuntr", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-sa", "senses": [{"gloss": "कुन्त्र् [kuntr], 1 P. To speak falsehood.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["kuntr"], "synonyms_slp1": ["kuntr"]}], "kunT": [{"id": "kunT", "headword": "कुन्थ्", "headword_slp1": "kunT", "fold": "kunT", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-sa", "senses": [{"gloss": "कुन्थ् [kunth], 1, 9 P. (कुन्थति, कुथ्नाति, कुन्थित)", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "To suffer pain.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "To cling to.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "To hurt.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["kunth"], "synonyms_slp1": ["kunth"]}], "kundaH": [{"id": "kundaH", "headword": "कुन्दः", "headword_slp1": "kundaH", "fold": "kundaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "apte-sa", "senses": [{"gloss": "कुन्दः [kundḥ] न्दम् [ndam], न्दम् [Uṇ.4.98] A kind of jasmine (white and delicate); कुन्दावदाताः कलहंसमालाः Bk.2.18; प्रातः कुन्दप्रसवशिथिलं जीवितं धारयेथाः Me.115; Ś.5.19. -न्दम् The flower of this plant; अलके बालकुन्दानुविद्धम् Me.67,49.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "न्दः An epithet of Viṣṇu.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "A fragrant oleander.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "One of the nine treasures of Kubera.", "gloss